-- title:
--   Crossings of the fibre at p ‖ M lie over the j-finite chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a nonzero $M$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image under `ZMod.unitsMap` for $M/p \mid M$ is $1$; assume $j$, in the form of the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ`, lies in the field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of full level. The data are: a morphism $\pi$ of $\mathrm{Spec}\,(R\,p)$-schemes $X_{\Gamma_M(M,H)} \to X_{\Gamma_N(p,M,H)}$ (a morphism commuting with the two structure maps `toBase`); an $R\,p$-algebra map $\iota_0$ from `chartAlgFin` at level $\Gamma_N$ to `chartAlgFin` at level $\Gamma_M$ (each the algebra of elements of the relevant $q$-expansion function field integral over the subalgebra generated by $j$) which is the identity on underlying Laurent series, with $\pi$ pinned on the $j$-finite charts, i.e. `ιFin` at level $\Gamma_M$ followed by $\pi$ equals $\mathrm{Spec}\,\iota_0$ followed by `ιFin` at level $\Gamma_N$; an automorphism $w$ of $X_{\Gamma_M(M,H)}$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,(R\,p)$ together with an $R\,p$-algebra automorphism $\theta$ of `chartAlgFin` at level $\Gamma_M$ satisfying $\theta(\iota_0 b)(q) = b(q^p)$ for all $b$ (the series of $\theta(\iota_0 b)$ is `qExpand ℚ p` applied to that of $b$) and pinning $w$ on the $j$-finite chart in the same sense; a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$, algebraically closed residue field of characteristic $p$, and a ring map $\rho : R\,p \to A$ compatible with $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; and two morphisms $\mathrm{comp}\,0, \mathrm{comp}\,1$ from the fibre at $\Gamma_N$ to the fibre at $\Gamma_M$ over the residue field of $A$ (fibres being the base changes of `toBase` along the residue map composed with $\rho$), both commuting with the projections to the base, both closed immersions, with $\mathrm{comp}\,0$ a section of the fibre map induced by $\pi$ and $\mathrm{comp}\,1$ obtained from $\mathrm{comp}\,0$ by the fibre map induced by $w$. The conclusion is that for every point $n$ of the fibre product of $\mathrm{comp}\,0$ and $\mathrm{comp}\,1$, the images of $n$ under either projection to the $\Gamma_N$-fibre, pushed forward to $X_{\Gamma_N(p,M,H)}$ by the first projection of that fibre, lie in the image of the base map of the $j$-finite chart `ιFin` at level $\Gamma_N$.
--
--   This is the statement that no point of the scheme-theoretic intersection of the two components of the Deligne–Rapoport special fibre at a prime dividing $M$ exactly once lies over the cusps, the two components being the section coming from the forgetful map and its Atkin–Lehner translate: both coordinates of each crossing lie over the $j$-finite chart. It feeds the construction of generic charts for the model at $p$ in [`ModularCurve.exists_xHDRModelAtP_atkinLehner_generic_chart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_xHDRModelAtP_atkinLehner_generic_chart).
